From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 09:43:03 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] alsa: prepare a stream again after its start failed

spa_alsa_start() prepares the PCM and, for playback without timer
scheduling (and for capture), starts it at once. When the driver
refuses that start, as Aurora's macaudio does for a speaker PCM while
speaker protection is not granted, spa_alsa_start() returned with the
stream not started but still marked prepared. spa_alsa_pause() leaves a
stream that never started alone, and so does spa_alsa_close(), so the
flag survived Suspend, close and reopen. Every later start skipped
do_prepare() and the silence it writes, and ALSA refused to start a
playback PCM with an empty buffer: -EPIPE on every start, for the life
of the node. On a MacBook Air (J413) one capture of the idle speaker
sink's monitor, started before any grant, left that sink unable to
start until PipeWire restarted.

Drop the stream and clear the prepared flag when the start fails, and
clear it when the PCM is closed.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c b/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c
index 3db6410..56fd1a8 100644
--- a/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c
+++ b/spa/plugins/alsa/alsa-pcm.c
@@ -1299,6 +1299,8 @@ int spa_alsa_close(struct state *state)
 	if ((err = snd_pcm_close(state->hndl)) < 0)
 		spa_log_warn(state->log, "%s: close failed: %s", state->name,
 				snd_strerror(err));
+	/* a reopened PCM is prepared again, whatever happened before the close */
+	state->prepared = false;
 
 	if (!state->disable_tsched)
 		spa_system_close(state->data_system, state->timerfd);
@@ -3981,7 +3983,7 @@ int spa_alsa_start(struct state *state)
 	 * goes off later */
 	if (state->stream == SND_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE) {
 		if ((err = do_start(state)) < 0)
-			return err;
+			goto not_started;
 	}
 
 	/* playback will start after first write. Without tsched, we start
@@ -3989,13 +3991,23 @@ int spa_alsa_start(struct state *state)
 	if (state->stream == SND_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK) {
 		if (state->disable_tsched || state->start_delay > 0)
 			if ((err = do_start(state)) < 0)
-				return err;
+				goto not_started;
 	}
 
 	state->started = true;
 	spa_loop_locked(state->data_loop, do_state_sync, 0, NULL, 0, state);
 
 	return 0;
+
+not_started:
+	/* The stream never started, so spa_alsa_pause() will not reset it:
+	 * drop it and prepare it again on the next start. Left prepared, the
+	 * next start skips do_prepare() and its silence, and a playback PCM
+	 * with an empty buffer refuses every start with -EPIPE until the node
+	 * is destroyed. */
+	do_drop(state);
+	state->prepared = false;
+	return err;
 }
 
 static struct state *find_state(uint32_t id)
